What is the finite-size analogue of that insight on a cache hierarchy with SIMD?
The best practical algorithm may look nothing like the proof while being directly inspired by it.
For example, the proof's frame idea has a very natural systems interpretation:

keep metadata describing the current logical layout;
permit several computational stages to operate against that layout;
compose address transformations symbolically;
materialize/reorder only when unavoidable;
fuse materialization with another pass that already touches every element.
That is basically compiler-style lazy layout transformation.
I'd be quite interested in letting an agent search for those fusion opportunities automatically in GMP's or FLINT's FFT multiplication path.

